backup
restore
logs
health check
storage
monitoring
upgrades

==================================================
82. DEPLOYMENT

Review production deployment.

Use the existing architecture.

Prefer:

Next.js
+
Python service/worker
+
PostgreSQL
+
protected storage

Do not introduce Kubernetes unless explicitly required.

==================================================
83. CONTAINERIZATION

If Docker is already part of the architecture:

ensure production images are clean.

If Docker is not currently used:

do not force Docker solely for this phase unless deployment requirements justify
it.

==================================================
84. PRODUCTION CONFIGURATION

Ensure:

debug disabled
secure cookies
HTTPS
production database
production storage
production logging

==================================================
85. DATABASE CONNECTION POOL

Configure sensible production connection pooling.

Do not use excessive connections.

Consider PostgreSQL server limits.

==================================================
86. TIMEOUTS

Configure reasonable:

HTTP timeout
database timeout
file operation timeout

Long document generation should use the worker architecture rather than
unlimited HTTP requests.

==================================================
87. WORKER RELIABILITY

If a worker is used:

ensure failed jobs do not disappear silently.

Record:

job status
error
timestamp

==================================================
88. JOB RETRIES

Retries should be limited.

Do not create infinite retry loops.

==================================================
89. SECURITY DEPENDENCY REVIEW

Review dependencies for:

known vulnerabilities
abandoned packages
unnecessary dependencies

Do not blindly upgrade every package.

Only upgrade when compatible.

==================================================
90. CODE QUALITY

Run:

lint
typecheck
tests
formatting

Remove:

unused code
debug statements
temporary scripts
development credentials

==================================================
91. API CONSISTENCY

Review API naming and response structures.

Do not have multiple inconsistent patterns.

==================================================
92. FRONTEND CONSISTENCY

Review:

buttons
dialogs
tables
forms
notifications
errors

Keep the interface simple.

Use consistent terminology:

Exam
Roster
Room
Seat
Template
Documents
Administration

==================================================
93. ACCESSIBILITY

Review:

keyboard navigation
focus states
form labels
table headers
dialog accessibility
color contrast
screen-reader labels

Do not use color alone for status.

==================================================
94. BROWSER SUPPORT

Support the browsers defined by the institutional environment.

Do not optimize for obsolete browsers unless required.

==================================================
95. SECURITY SCANNING

Run available:

dependency audit
static analysis
secret scanning

Do not commit generated reports containing secrets.

==================================================
96. PERFORMANCE TEST

Use synthetic data:

500 students
10 rooms

Test:

roster import
seating
document generation
package generation

Measure:

execution time
memory
disk usage

Do not optimize prematurely.

==================================================
97. LOAD TEST

If practical:

simulate multiple authorized users accessing the dashboard.

Do not perform aggressive load testing against production.

